id: pm-rlm-sync-changelog
title: Keep sync changelog regeneration consistent with the release gate
description: ""
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[2]: automation,changelog
created_at: "2026-11-08T03:19:32.680Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-09T23:41:06.852Z"
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: The configured sync generation and package changelog check agree on real temporary trackers; Keep dependency pins and all coverage thresholds unchanged and record a behavioral revert failure
comments[22]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-08T03:19:49.208Z",pi-agent,"PR #57 reaches changelog verification after its tests pass. The reusable workflow injects --no-pending-release for its default changelog:full script, but the package checker expects its ordinary full generation. Select a caller-owned changelog:automation alias to preserve the canonical policy and compare real generated bytes with the existing check in a temporary tracker. REST refresh alone cannot repair this mismatch. Dependency pins, thresholds, native item histories and the delegated changelog implementation remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-08T03:25:50.115Z",pi-agent,"The real temporary-tracker regression passes 1 of 1 and local typecheck passes. In a disposable copy, reverting only the caller post-import-script selection fails the existing changelog check, while restoring it passes 1 of 1. The exact pinned reusable workflow declares the string input and conditionally adds the differing flag only for its default changelog:full name. Node test concurrency remains capped at two. Full npm and Bun release checks will run sequentially after the focused verification."
  "2026-11-08T04:07:42.542Z",pi-agent,"The final real-tracker fixture clears inherited Git repository selection, PM-root overrides, npm user-config policy variants and Node test context before setting its isolated paths. Credential-shaped keys are removed. The refined fixture still passes 1 of 1 and typecheck passes. Product configuration, dependency pins and thresholds are unchanged."
  "2026-11-08T06:15:10.112Z",pi-agent,"Focused regression, local typecheck and isolated behavioral revert pass. Full npm and Bun release checks remain required at unchanged thresholds; final-head CI is the full gate and is not yet confirmed. The serial local release queue continues separately."
  "2026-11-08T06:15:19.089Z",pi-agent,"Review handoff: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/pull/60. Final CI is visible at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/pull/60/checks. Focused regression, local typecheck and behavioral revert pass. Full npm/Bun gates are pending final-head CI confirmation, not approved. All tracker writes are completed before final-head CI observation. Release this agent claim for orchestrator verification; the item stays in progress."
  "2026-11-09T16:57:00.593Z",codex-agent,"Continuation audit: the existing PR is #60 and the prior agent already merged current main locally. One unresolved review thread PRRT_kwDOVOym8860_NwH identifies the PR #57 issue-ownership tag. Verify it against the sync refresh selector, remove it through the pinned CLI, preserve its historical PR reference, and add a revert-sensitive regression. The latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Keep all prior append-only history and the existing item; no duplicate PR or item."
  "2026-11-09T16:59:13.630Z",codex-agent,"Verified thread PRRT_kwDOVOym8860_NwH: GitHub identifies #57 as a PR, and the pinned pm-github refresh selector converts gh provenance tags into issue(number:) queries. Removed only gh:unbraind/pm-rlm#57 with the pinned CLI; retained the existing PR #57 comments and append-only history. Self-review of the entire PR diff found no additional ownership-tag instance. Regression: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/automation-changelog.test.ts passes 2/2; the linked pm test passes 1/1 commands, 2/2 tests. Disposable-copy revert proof: restoring only the pre-fix item makes the ownership test fail (1 pass, 1 fail); restoring the fix passes 2/2. Reverting only post-import-script selection makes the real changelog check fail (1 pass, 1 fail); restoring it passes 2/2. Typecheck and lint pass; isolated strict tracker health with required merge drivers exits 0, history drift and integrity checks pass, and no pending merge receipt exists. The normal shell discovers an unrelated newer global extension; a fresh HOME removes that local version-skew finding without changing tracked settings. Prior manual release CI took about 20 minutes per job; full local gates will run sequentially within a bounded budget, otherwise current-head CI remains the full certification boundary."
  "2026-11-09T17:19:23.302Z",codex-agent,"Final review evidence for PRRT_kwDOVOym8860_NwH: an additional disposable-copy proof restores ONLY the incorrect provenance tag, preserving every other byte of the fixed item. The ownership regression passes 1/1 before reversion, fails 0/1 with that tag restored, and passes 1/1 after restoring the fix. Exact focused proof command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"work item\" test/automation-changelog.test.ts. The complete focused file passes 2/2, and the linked pm test passes 1/1 commands. npm run typecheck and npm run lint pass. npm run test:install passes 4/4 with zero skips or cancellations: packed npm and Bun consumers plus repair through both global-symlink layouts. npm run verify:release-publish-attestation passes. Identity, duplication, build and docstring gates passed during the optional npm release attempt. That attempt was stopped after about 13 minutes without certifying the full gate: its final test summary is 260 passed, 0 failed, 23 canceled. The stopped process group has no remaining active process and incomplete ignored coverage output was removed. Bun full release was not run; the full npm/Bun certification remains delegated to final-head CI at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/pull/60/checks. All existing thresholds and dependency pins are preserved relative to current main. Release this agent claim after recording evidence, retain in_progress for orchestrator verification, and regenerate/check the changelog after this last tracker mutation. No review-thread replies, resolutions, reactions, merge or release were performed."
  "2026-11-09T17:58:53.226Z",codex-agent,"Continuation audit preserves the clean remote head and existing PR #60. Current main is already merged. General rule: issue-sync ownership fields must identify GitHub issues, never pull requests; historical PR references remain audit context. The existing regression checks only one tag. Audit every current tracker item and ownership representation, strengthen the regression across the package, and prove adversarial tag and github_url mutations fail in a disposable copy. Existing CodeRabbit thread PRRT_kwDOVOym8860_NwH has no additional comments or outside-diff findings."
  "2026-11-09T18:01:47.317Z",codex-agent,"Class-wide audit: GitHub all-status issue responses identify PRs #20, #33, #35 and #58 as additional false issue owners. Removed all four tags from pm-rlm-disagreement, pm-rlm-b602 and pm-rlm-toolchain-1104 with pinned pm updates; preserved references and histories. All 41 current native documents and every gh tag, github_url, github_number and leading issue declaration are checked against independently verified issue identities (local issues #4/#5/#37/#38/#42/#49 and upstream issue #1609). Non-git temporary tracker SDK and full unbounded CLI JSON/TOON reads retain the same ownership fields. The package does not implement GitHub sync ownership selection; runtime SDK/CLI source has no such selector, and the packed allowlist excludes the package tracker. Existing packed acceptance still covers both consumers. Focused files pass 5/5. Disposable-copy revert proof: restoring only each removed tag (#57, #20, #33, #35, #58), independently, makes the package-wide native regression fail; injecting github_url or github_number for PR #57 into another item also fails. Fixed corpus passes before and after all seven mutations. Exact proof test: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"every native\" test/issue-ownership.test.ts. No existing test or threshold was weakened. Full npm and Bun gates will run sequentially with at most two workers."
  "2026-11-09T18:07:03.598Z",codex-agent,"Final regression refinement keeps future legitimate issue imports working: the offline oracle rejects all PR identities in the exhaustive public package snapshot (numbers 1 through 63), permits independently verified upstream issue #1609 and future unknown issue numbers, and preserves ordinary PR prose and pr tags. This proves the ownership classification on the complete audited domain without claiming to classify future GitHub records. Final focused command node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/issue-ownership.test.ts test/automation-changelog.test.ts passes 5/5; typecheck and lint pass. Repeated all seven isolated mutations against this final test implementation: five tag restorations and github_url/github_number injection each fail the native corpus regression, and both fixed-corpus controls pass. All changed history files are byte-prefix extensions of current main. Isolated strict pm health with required merge drivers passes. No pm CLI/SDK defect was encountered; a rejected ambiguous file-list argument was corrected by repeating --add."
  "2026-11-09T18:38:11.758Z",codex-agent,"Final-source npm release:check attempt reached its 1450-second local bound under high shared-host load: 262 tests passed, 0 failed, 24 canceled. The final ownership regression ran and passed inside that suite. Identity, typecheck, lint, duplication, build and docstring gates passed before coverage. This is incomplete full-gate and coverage evidence, not a successful certification or a demonstrated assertion failure. The npm process group has no active descendants. Bun release:check now runs sequentially with the same two-worker cap. An earlier local wrapper was superseded and stopped after the regression was refined; only this final-source run is reported as current evidence."
  "2026-11-09T19:10:28.233Z",codex-agent,"Final handoff for PR #60 and thread PRRT_kwDOVOym8860_NwH: preserve the earlier #57 fix and close the class by removing four more PR ownership tags (#20, #33, #35, #58) through pinned pm updates. All five independent tag-only reversions fail the package-wide regression; github_url and github_number injections fail too; restored controls pass. Final linked pm tests pass 2/2 commands (5/5 tests). npm run test:install passes 4/4 packed npm/Bun and repair-layout cases, with zero failures, cancellations or skips. npm run audit:prod reports zero vulnerabilities; release attestation, typecheck, lint, duplication, build, docstring and changelog checks pass. Both final-source full release attempts were bounded at 1450 seconds each: npm 262 passed, 0 failed, 24 canceled; Bun 263 passed, 0 failed, 23 canceled. Full coverage and release certification remain incomplete and require final-head CI at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/pull/60/checks. Both full-gate process groups exited, and incomplete ignored coverage output was removed. The remote branch and main were refreshed and remain unchanged. No dependency pin, threshold or existing test was weakened. The ownership oracle exhaustively covers the verified public snapshot through number 63 and allows future unknown issue imports. No pm CLI/SDK defect was found. Release this agent claim and retain in_progress for orchestrator verification; no thread replies, resolutions, merge or release were performed."
  "2026-11-09T21:11:40.879Z",codex-agent,"Re-review round 2 (auto) blocked PR #60 with two findings, both verified valid: (blocking) the automation fixture passes the npm shim path to a Node subprocess, which cannot execute on a Windows checkout because npm installs platform shims there; (non-blocking) the ownership oracle pins the /pull/ URL rejection only for the github_url field, so a declaration-regex change could silently drop the same rejection for description declarations. General rules: (1) pm CLI invocations from Node tests must target the package JavaScript entrypoint, never the npm shim directory, whether passed as a Node argument or spawned as a command without a shell; (2) every ownership field that can carry a GitHub URL needs an adversarial pull-request rejection case in the oracle. Package-wide audit found thirteen shim invocations across eleven test files plus two packed-consumer shim commands; all will be fixed, with a source-scan property test that fails if any instance returns. Self-review also ports the sibling round's quoting-style YAML read and delivered-fixture assertion for the same test file so the next review is clean. No thresholds, pins or existing tests are weakened."
  "2026-11-09T21:11:44.221Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 plan: fix every pm CLI invocation to use the package JavaScript entrypoint (13 execPath-argument instances plus 2 packed-consumer command instances), add a package-wide source-scan property test for the shim anti-pattern, add both declaration-form pull-URL rejection cases to the ownership oracle, and read the sync post-import script as YAML with a quoting-style property test plus a delivered-fixture changelog assertion. Focused gates for every changed file, then typecheck, lint, duplication, docstring, identity and changelog gates at unchanged thresholds; full local release attempts bounded by host load with final-head CI as the certification boundary."
  "2026-11-09T21:38:00.959Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 fixes complete. Thread PRRT_kwDOVOym8861cNqF (blocking): every pm CLI invocation now targets the package JavaScript entrypoint instead of the npm shim directory - 13 execPath-argument instances across ten test files plus 2 packed-consumer command instances in the install acceptance; a new source-scan property test (test/pm-entrypoint.test.ts) scans every test and script source with a must-refuse corpus (path-segment and join-part spellings) and a must-allow corpus (bind calls, PATH construction, package-manager args), so ANY re-introduced instance fails. Thread PRRT_kwDOVOym8861cNqQ (non-blocking): the ownership oracle now rejects pull-request URLs in BOTH declaration forms (GitHub issue and imported GH issue) for every number in the verified snapshot, pinning the must-identify-an-issue rejection against silent regex changes. Self-review also ported the sibling round's quoting-style YAML read of post-import-script (the regex fell back to the default for single-quoted or unquoted values) and the delivered-fixture changelog assertion. Disposable-copy revert proofs, each restored byte-identical and re-passed: (1) restoring only the npm shim on one line makes the new property test fail naming that file, the fixed line passes; (2) narrowing the declaration regex to issue URLs only, the exact silent-drop change the thread describes, makes the oracle fail at the new pull-declaration case with Missing expected exception, while the pre-round test suite passed with that mutation; (3) reverting the YAML read to the regex extraction fails the quoting-style test on single-quoted and unquoted values; (4) making the fixture item open, so generation silently omits it while the byte check still passes, fails the new Synthetic delivered change assertion while the old heading-only assertion passed. Focused gates: 101 tests pass across every changed test file (7+42+28+24), packed npm and Bun consumers plus both global-symlink repair layouts pass 4/4, typecheck, lint, duplication (0 percent, threshold 0) and docstring gates pass. No existing test, threshold or dependency pin was weakened."
  "2026-11-09T22:26:06.744Z",codex-agent,"Continuation verified the existing branch and remote head f670a63, existing tracker item, both unresolved review threads and the latest review body (no outside-diff findings). Main is already merged. Preserving the predecessor changes and append-only evidence; independently checking the cross-platform entrypoint rule, ownership-declaration oracle, revert proofs and sequential full npm/Bun gates with at most two workers."
  "2026-11-09T22:26:52.413Z",codex-agent,"Class audit found four remaining executable shim overrides in the changelog, changelog:full, changelog:check and release:notes package scripts. Removed those overrides: the pinned pm-changelog resolver already reads the installed PM package bin manifest and invokes its JavaScript target through the current Node executable. Expanded the adversarial source scan to production sources, scripts, examples, all test helpers, root TypeScript and every package script. Ownership validation is shared across native, SDK, JSON/TOON and non-git reads; both declaration syntaxes now exercise all 63 snapshot numbers. No production source uses a PM shim. Packed acceptance retains real npm/Bun manager entrypoints and also exercises the explicit JavaScript bin."
  "2026-11-09T22:28:46.072Z",codex-agent,"Independent disposable-copy revert proof: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/pm-entrypoint.test.ts passed before and after restoring each of all 19 historical shim invocations separately (13 Node-argument uses, 2 packed-consumer command uses, 4 package-script overrides); every mutation failed and identified its file or script. node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"ownership oracle\" test/issue-ownership.test.ts passed before and after narrowing only the declaration extraction regex to issues URLs; that mutation failed with Missing expected exception on the new pull-declaration corpus. General rules: platform launchers must not substitute for JavaScript executable entrypoints; an ownership oracle must reject invalid declarations instead of silently dropping them. The unchanged broad declaration parser remains deliberate: restricting it to issues URLs would hide invalid pull declarations. Both description prefixes cover all 63 known numbers, alongside valid issues, future issues, external ownership and historical PR references. The Ubuntu-only CI shell step uses its Unix launcher correctly; it is outside the faulty Node/subprocess invocation class."
  "2026-11-09T22:39:19.535Z",codex-agent,"Independent focused verification completed: pm test pm-rlm-sync-changelog --run --progress --timeout 900 passes all 7 linked commands, 111 test executions including repeated core regressions; the distinct changed-file batches pass 101 tests (7 + 42 + 28 + 24), and packed npm/Bun installation plus both global-symlink repair layouts pass 4/4, with zero skipped, canceled or failed tests. npm run typecheck, npm run lint, npm run duplication (zero percent), npm run docstring, npm run changelog:full, npm run changelog:check and npm run verify:release-publish-attestation pass. Strict tracker health and required merge drivers pass with a fresh HOME; the ambient HOME alone discovers a globally installed pm-github requiring a newer host, so full gates will use the required isolated HOME and clean Git configuration. All four changed histories preserve main byte prefixes, and this item preserves the previous branch head. Committing the source and tracker evidence before full npm and Bun release checks so their shallow HEAD clones include the fixes. Full checks will run sequentially, each at unchanged thresholds and at most two workers, with a 30-minute local bound per wrapper."
  "2026-11-09T23:09:55.818Z",codex-agent,"Full npm release:check on source commit ac18ae0 reached its 1800-second local bound with 419 tests passed, 0 failed, 15 canceled and 0 skipped (434 reported tests). No assertion failure marker was emitted. Identity, typecheck, lint, duplication, build and docstring stages passed before coverage. The interrupted coverage/full release check is incomplete evidence, not approval. Its process group was stopped and incomplete coverage output removed. The Bun release:check wrapper now runs sequentially on the same committed source, using a fresh HOME, clean Git configuration, unchanged thresholds and at most two workers. Exact-head CI remains required for complete release certification."
  "2026-11-09T23:41:05.639Z",codex-agent,"Final committed-source verification for ac18ae0: all 19 historical shim invocations independently fail the package-wide guard when restored, and the fixed control passes before and after. A disposable dependency layout containing a non-JavaScript npm launcher also passes the real configured-sync fixture with the fix; restoring ONLY the init invocation or ONLY the create invocation independently fails with SyntaxError, and the restored control passes. Runtime proof command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"configured sync regeneration\" test/automation-changelog.test.ts. Narrowing ONLY the ownership declaration extraction to issues URLs fails the ownership-oracle test with Missing expected exception; the restored parser passes. RegExp.exec is a regular-expression receiver, not shell execution; retaining broad extraction is necessary to reject malformed declarations rather than ignore them. Both description prefixes exercise every number in the 63-number snapshot. Full wrappers ran sequentially with two workers and unchanged thresholds, each bounded at 1800 seconds: npm reported 419 passed, 0 failed, 15 canceled, 0 skipped; Bun logged 393 successful parent/nested test records and zero assertion-failure markers but was interrupted before a terminal summary. Both full release/coverage certifications remain incomplete and require final-head CI at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/pull/60/checks. Both process groups stopped and incomplete coverage was removed. Independent focused batches pass 101 distinct tests, all 7 linked commands pass, and packed npm/Bun plus both global-symlink layouts pass 4/4 with no skips or cancellations. Production audit now reports zero vulnerabilities and pack dry-run passes (138 files). Typecheck, lint, zero-duplication, build, docstrings, changelog, release attestation and isolated-HOME strict tracker health passed. Remote refresh confirms main is already merged and the existing PR branch has no competing update. No dependency, threshold or existing test was weakened, and no new PM CLI/SDK defect was identified. Both review threads are fixed by ac18ae0; leave their responses and resolution to the orchestrator. Release this claim and retain in_progress for verification; no PR merge or release is authorized."
